:1,"x":25,"y":24},{"type":2,"army":1,"x":31,"y":24},{"type":3,"army":0,"x":1,"y":25},{"type":40,"army":0,"x":3,"y":25},{"type":3,"army":1,"x":15,"y":25},{"type":52,"army":1,"x":39,"y":25,"cargo":[3,3]},{"type":8,"army":0,"x":2,"y":26},{"type":17,"army":1,"x":22,"y":26},{"type":39,"army":1,"x":32,"y":26},{"type":9,"army":0,"x":1,"y":27},{"type":51,"army":1,"x":25,"y":27},{"type":51,"army":1,"x":31,"y":27},{"type":39,"army":0,"x":2,"y":28},{"type":33,"army":1,"x":27,"y":28}],"arrivals":[{"turn":3,"army":1,"units":[{"type":40,"x":44,"y":13},{"type":40,"x":44,"y":18},{"type":49,"x":44,"y":11},{"type":49,"x":44,"y":20}]},{"turn":5,"army":1,"units":[{"type":33,"x":44,"y":15},{"type":49,"x":44,"y":10},{"type":49,"x":44,"y":21}]},{"turn":8,"army":1,"units":[{"type":49,"x":44,"y":12},{"type":49,"x":44,"y":19},{"type":3,"x":44,"y":14},{"type":3,"x":44,"y":17},{"type":45,"x":44,"y":15},{"type":47,"x":44,"y":16}]}],"objective":{"kind":"fortress"},"general":{"x":1,"y":2},"turnLimit":30,"cap":22,"music":21,"briefing":"The Gate of Eden.\n\nEvery road to Olympos runs through here, and the Union has shut it. The blockade fortress is a maze: an outer wall, chambers of open deck where nothing can hide, gates two hexes wide with mines in them, and at the centre the Carthago, a fortress built to stop a fleet.\n\nThe docks inside the walls are full of Talos. Their beams will cut us apart on the decks, but not in the magnetic river along our side of the approach: hold there, then go in gate by gate. The comet debris west of the walls is the best cover in the sector; a ship that enters it stops there.\n\nThe Union's reserve is east of the Gate and will come through on the fourth turn, the sixth and the ninth. Destroy the Carthago and the road to Olympos is open.","goal":"Destroy the Carthago fortress at the heart of the Gate.","guards":3,"chapter":"Chapter 8 · The Gate of Eden","transmission":"The Gate has held for forty years. It only has to hold for one more day. That is all the time I need.","strategy":["Advance through the magnetic river on your side of the approach: the Talos beams can't reach you there. Use the comet debris as stepping stones, but remember a ship that enters it stops.","Go in gate by gate. The gates are two hexes wide and mined: clear the Wisps with ranged fire first.","The dock beside the Carthago is full of Talos. Bring it to zero early, before it empties onto the decks.","Reserves come from the east on turns 4, 6 and 9. Hold the inner walls against them, and send everything else at the Carthago.","Pandoras guard two of the gates, Echidna and Rockeye pods hold the walls, and the turn 9 reserve brings an Msnp-II and an Msfb-5 bomber. Kill the bombers first."],"plan":[{"n":2,"path":[[3,4],[9,5],[14,6]]},{"n":1,"path":[[3,15],[9,15],[14,15]]},{"n":2,"path":[[3,26],[9,25],[14,24]]},{"n":3,"path":[[18,15],[26,15]]},{"n":4,"at":[42,15],"note":"Reserves T4 · T6 · T9"}]}